<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss</id><updated>2026-09-01T05:21:01Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Middle East live: Oil prices extend gains as US-Iran tensions flare again</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5e9ec657983fa00dbcd976b1d046b0797ef4ef607ca2185f4cc4e8c85a84561b</id><updated>2026-09-01T05:21:01Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T03:38:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260901-middle-east-live-oil-prices-extend-gains-as-us-iran-tensions-flare-again" /><summary type="html">Oil prices rose further Tuesday as renewed military exchanges between the United States and Iran, coupled with Donald Trump’s vow to hit Tehran “hard,” fueled fears of a broader escalation after weeks of relative calm. Follow our live blog for the latest developments.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Trump threatens to ‘hit Iran hard’ as strikes resume after month-long lull</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6c17b672b518187c844e017b262f2a61fc4bfb0a712e3c22221bf2d9972e54ea</id><updated>2026-09-01T05:21:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T20:36:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260831-trump-threatens-to-hit-iran-hard-as-strikes-resume-after-month-long-lull--926c2ca9c70e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260831-trump-threatens-to-hit-iran-hard-as-strikes-resume-after-month-long-lull" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump said Monday that the US would hit back against Iranian attacks on US targets in the Middle East, according to a Fox News reporter. The Iranian attacks were themselves a response to US strikes on an island in the Strait of Hormuz, the first flare-up in a month.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Trump vows to hit back 'hard' after first exchange of fire with Iran in weeks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:47c8bf7c4ac6f7736c2333f270d379cbfeea0e1875f2581937bbeeac116eadac</id><updated>2026-09-01T05:21:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T18:37:10Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/trump-vows-to-hit-back-hard-after-first-exchange-of-fire-with-iran-in-weeks--7701c0e7ac56.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/trump-vows-to-hit-back-hard-after-first-exchange-of-fire-with-iran-in-weeks" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump threatened to hit Iran "hard" after the two foes traded fire for the first time in over a month, while Iran's president warned that more fighting with the US was not in his country's interest. After six months of war, the foes remain at an impasse, with Iran keeping the strategic Strait of Hormuz closed and the US persisting with a naval counter-blockade of Iran. FRANCE 24's Reza Sayah reports from Tehran.</summary></entry><entry><title>Raising the Altalena: Netanyahu digs up sunken 1948 arms ship in ‘pre-election stunt’</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e57bdb4731ce3eba1cab67e6854715a53365a92a25422cc52ba6d1d8224db785</id><updated>2026-09-01T05:21:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T16:54:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260831-raising-altalena-netanyahu-digs-up-sunken-1948-arms-ship-irgun-pre-election-stunt--b62ae1447324.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260831-raising-altalena-netanyahu-digs-up-sunken-1948-arms-ship-irgun-pre-election-stunt" /><summary type="html">A ship carrying arms for a right-wing militia, the Altalena was sunk 78 years ago off the coast of Tel Aviv at the orders of Israel’s founders. The discovery of its wreckage last week has given the country’s right-wing government ammunition to target the left and attempt to redirect the campaign for legislative elections in October.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Latest flare-up between US and Iran bring conflict's lull to an end</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e72b6d549489ed9bf56347cd1f540188e50b2e0497210bdd99b8828bf57b8b71</id><updated>2026-09-01T05:21:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T15:33:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/latest-flare-up-between-us-and-iran-bring-conflict-s-lull-to-an-end--9f77617ac27c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/latest-flare-up-between-us-and-iran-bring-conflict-s-lull-to-an-end" /><summary type="html">Iran's foreign minister has accused Israel's Benjamin Netanyahu of tricking the United States into war with the Islamic Republic. Over six months into the conflict, there appears to be no end in sight. This after the US struck sites in Iran, prompting Tehran to respond. An April ceasefire brought an end to intense fighting, but sporadic attacks have continued over the Strait of Hormuz. Tehran's closure of the waterway during the conflict has pressured global oil markets, and in turn Donald Trump at home.</summary></entry><entry><title>Strait of Hormuz accessibility at the centre of US-Iran war flare-up</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9591061c105dc782f5897058740df697de31af1cfeea537398901c8505e4c119</id><updated>2026-09-01T05:21:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T12:47:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/strait-of-hormuz-accessibility-at-the-centre-of-us-iran-war-flare-up--9de5d0383172.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/strait-of-hormuz-accessibility-at-the-centre-of-us-iran-war-flare-up" /><summary type="html">For the first time in a month, the US has launched strikes against Iran. The attack targeted the shipping island of Larak in the Strait of Hormuz. The US says it was aimed at preventing Tehran from placing sea mines in the strategic shipping lane, just days after Washington announced it had completed clearing explosives from there. Iran then reiterated its attacks, saying it had struck two US military bases in Jordan. FRANCE 24's Rochelle Ferguson-Bouyahi tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Relentless heat worsens Gaza's ongoing struggle to access water</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6c61c5cebc2966400070d40a5962eefb8e6a0498ca56827e34c5c0389cb42233</id><updated>2026-09-01T05:21:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T10:49:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/relentless-heat-worsens-gaza-s-ongoing-struggle-to-access-water--85e6fae055ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/relentless-heat-worsens-gaza-s-ongoing-struggle-to-access-water" /><summary type="html">In Gaza, securing drinking water is a relentless daily struggle. The war with Israel has destroyed critical water and sanitation infrastructure, and as temperatures soar, the extreme heat is escalating an already severe shortage into a deadly humanitarian crisis. Two and a half years of war with Israel have damaged or destroyed nearly 90% of Gaza’s water and sanitation infrastructure according to UNICEF.</summary></entry><entry><title>Iran, US trade fire in first exchange in a month</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:91b0c84526e42d44ae29198cb1d7ab7b7bee3ea2e79f8793e20c57eb1145b1d9</id><updated>2026-09-01T05:21:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T10:49:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260831-iran-us-trade-fire-in-first-exchange-in-a-month--237ef98b8b75.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260831-iran-us-trade-fire-in-first-exchange-in-a-month" /><summary type="html">Iran attacked US military targets in the Middle East on Monday in retaliation following American strikes on an island in the Strait of Hormuz, the first exchange of fire for a month in a war that has engulfed the region.</summary></entry><entry><title>Middle East war flares up after Iran responds to US attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c2226520fcdd2dcf3deaa92a495b6d3b0e886d8302cec3940de8741ed27a255c</id><updated>2026-09-01T05:21:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T10:43:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east-war-flares-up-after-iran-responds-to-us-attacks--d008a7b9fca7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east-war-flares-up-after-iran-responds-to-us-attacks" /><summary type="html">Iran attacked US military targets in the Middle East in retaliation for the first American strikes on its territory in a month. This signs a fresh flare-up of the war that has engulfed the region. Washington said its attacks were aimed at preventing Iran from placing more sea mines in the strait and as it threatens new secondary economic sanctions. FRANCE 24's Reza Sayah is in Tehran and tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>US renews attack on Iran while threatening financial sanctions on Tehran allies</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa71496c6ba2a00613342b2e4738dd05a0e5af91f469d5817448ed9fbe7d6ff8</id><updated>2026-09-01T05:21:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T09:40:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-renews-attack-on-iran-while-threatening-financial-sanctions-on-tehran-allies--8d1a4f56eab1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-renews-attack-on-iran-while-threatening-financial-sanctions-on-tehran-allies" /><summary type="html">Hostilities between the US and Iran resumed after a month's pause. The US said Iran was preparing to launch sea mines into the Strait of Hormuz. Iran retaliated by hitting US military bases in Jordan. Meanwhile, the US Treasury Secretary said there would be more economic sanctions on the way for banks doing business with Iran.</summary></entry><entry><title>Iran says continuing war ‘not in our interest’ after fighting flares</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7798eb42f1e95b36dd3393d8f4c5b9964f182c9e83aab9b222db7cfa034d556e</id><updated>2026-09-01T05:21:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T23:02:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260830-middle-east-live-us-strikes-iran-for-first-time-in-a-month--572426b25307.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260830-middle-east-live-us-strikes-iran-for-first-time-in-a-month" /><summary type="html">Iranian President Masoud Pezeshkian said Monday that continuing the war with the United States was not in his country's interest, following a fresh military flare-up between the two countries after a month-long lull. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>US forces strike Iranian launchers on Larak island in Strait of Hormuz</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:74092eb25b59c198efbaefe4cf6da07cf18abced9cece9cab2f56476de31d96c</id><updated>2026-09-01T05:21:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T20:27:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260830-us-forces-strike-iranian-launchers-on-larak-island-in-strait-of-hormuz--1eaea36d941e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260830-us-forces-strike-iranian-launchers-on-larak-island-in-strait-of-hormuz" /><summary type="html">US forces struck Iranian rocket launchers on the Strait of Hormuz in the first military action in a month, a US official said Sunday. ⁠Iran's ⁠Revolutionary ​Guards ​said the attack on Larak ​island ‌killed and wounded ⁠several Iranian fighters and ​civilians, and ‌vowed to punish those ​responsible.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu condemns violence in West Bank</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc97542ccc1d8e586a2a1ba963d1bf3fd130723c0e37a9fbbbbccaed99b2b862</id><updated>2026-09-01T05:21:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T08:46:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/netanyahu-condemns-violence-in-west-bank--f146c0bf0b9a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/netanyahu-condemns-violence-in-west-bank" /><summary type="html">It was a rare condemnation from what is widely seen as the most religious and ultranationalist government in Israel’s history. Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu condemned recent attacks by Israeli settlers on Palestinians in the occupied West Bank, but described the violence as the actions of a “handful of rioters.” Tensions have surged across the territory, with activists accusing settlers of acting with impunity. Much of the recent violence has taken place in the town of Qusra. Peter O’Brien reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu condemns 'criminal acts of violence' by settlers in West Bank villages</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:348364db68f0f9b34fc60e3125a60992e3eac99862821e0cd1deb99f5cd89cae</id><updated>2026-09-01T05:21:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T18:34:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260829-netanyahu-condemns-criminal-acts-of-violence-by-settlers-in-west-bank-villages--94a13b44b42b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260829-netanyahu-condemns-criminal-acts-of-violence-by-settlers-in-west-bank-villages" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on Saturday condemned what he called "criminal acts of violence" perpetrated by Israeli settlers in two Palestinian villages. Earlier in August, a group of settlers blocked supplies from entering Palestinian houses on the outskirts of Qusra and attacked a Palestinian family and a foreign media crew in nearby Jalud.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran war reaches 6-month mark: Conflict cost $1,100 per US taxpayer</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9a4922d40e09c8b3d26390b420be9af073f405a7eeb5c32f0d3ebb4f4538ec54</id><updated>2026-09-01T05:21:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T15:24:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/iran-war-reaches-6-month-mark-conflict-cost-1-100-per-us-taxpayer--0914f5e1ed99.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/iran-war-reaches-6-month-mark-conflict-cost-1-100-per-us-taxpayer" /><summary type="html">After six months of war, Iran’s leadership has coalesced around a hard core of military generals and clerics long entrenched in the ruling theocracy. They are ready for a potentially long confrontation with the US and determined to prevent any unrest at home. It’s a far cry from US President Donald Trump’s initial hopes of toppling the Islamic Republic and his subsequent claims that “regime change” had brought more compromising officials to the fore. In an analysis, FRANCE 24's Philip Turle said the war had so far cost around 1,100 US dollars for each US taxpayer.</summary></entry><entry><title>Situation in Niger 'not stabilised yet' as security forces deploy around airport</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0bea67327cf9280d51b5cd021631209eaf33acc6941f6b2f23f334f6e0c0cddd</id><updated>2026-09-01T05:21:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T13:59:17Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/situation-in-niger-not-stabilised-yet-as-security-forces-deploy-around-airport--ef7479b2be5d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/situation-in-niger-not-stabilised-yet-as-security-forces-deploy-around-airport" /><summary type="html">A group of soldiers in Niger rebelled against officers at a key military base and fired at sensitive locations in the capital, Niamey, in an apparent mutiny marked by gunfire and explosions, authorities said Saturday, in what was seen as a major threat to the country's struggling junta. FRANCE 24's Wassim Nasr brings you this analysis.</summary></entry><entry><title>Several killed in Israeli strikes on Gaza and West Bank</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5ba1a8b8383e10e3667797aab9a595f9ba1fcf6866f06600c9b490f4bd27eab9</id><updated>2026-09-01T05:21:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T10:34:58Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/several-killed-in-israeli-strikes-on-gaza-and-west-bank--999317521e97.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/several-killed-in-israeli-strikes-on-gaza-and-west-bank" /><summary type="html">Israeli strikes in Gaza have killed five people, local hospital officials said Friday. Two brothers and another relative died in a strike on the family’s home outside Khan Younis, officials at Nasser Hospital said. Two separate Israeli strikes killed one person each in Gaza City, according to health officials at Shifa hospital.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel army carries out rare West Bank air strike, killing 'three terrorists'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f88ca6257a667aad17f5f010932040772e0d3503ee12f74af78226cb01f0250e</id><updated>2026-09-01T05:21:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T17:14:47Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260828-israel-army-carries-out-rare-west-bank-air-strike-killing-three-terrorists--652d71ff42af.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260828-israel-army-carries-out-rare-west-bank-air-strike-killing-three-terrorists" /><summary type="html">Israel's military said it carried out an air strike in the Jenin area in the West Bank on Friday that killed a ​Palestinian it described as a Hamas militant operative as well as two of his accomplices, in a rare use of deadly Israeli air power in the occupied territory.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>There is no proof that this video shows a plane crash in Tel Aviv</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5d8dc2573215467a78e8bee7d3bbe1158619f598a8cb68058399fc35231d248a</id><updated>2026-09-01T05:21:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T15:31:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260828-no-proof-video-shows-plane-crash-tel-aviv--6a155fc46fc5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260828-no-proof-video-shows-plane-crash-tel-aviv" /><summary type="html">A video showing an airplane rammed into the side of a building has been circulating widely on social media. While social media users are claiming that the video shows a plane that crashed in Tel Aviv after an Iranian attack, its origin remains unknown and its authenticity highly questionable.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel's 'retrospective incrimination: First we shoot, we kill &amp; then find a reason why it happened'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:77ef7b4bae090098efb124065b7dad921b8804a297327ede3a96c5ae20c66300</id><updated>2026-09-01T05:21:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-28T08:58:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/retrospective-incrimination-first-we-shoot-we-kill-and-then-we-find-a-reason-why-it-happened--b52d3a0f8d9e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/retrospective-incrimination-first-we-shoot-we-kill-and-then-we-find-a-reason-why-it-happened" /><summary type="html">Liza Kaminov is pleased to welcome Nadav Weiman, Executive Director of Breaking the Silence. He says there is a troubling gap between how Israeli military operations in Gaza are publicly explained and what soldiers experience on the ground. Testimonies collected by Breaking the Silence suggest that this gap is not simply about individual incidents, but about the policies, assumptions and rules of engagement. The testimony surrounding the Nasser Hospital strike points to “retrospective incrimination”: rather than identifying a legitimate military target before an attack, evidence connecting those killed to Hamas may be sought afterward in order to justify the strike.</summary></entry><entry><title>Syria President appoints Kurdish leader Mazloum Abdi as presidential adviser</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:05f84eb643e9fcedd290b281e84401d309c899d098ac48b75d00c5f222675e14</id><updated>2026-09-01T05:21:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T21:59:11Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260827-syria-president-appoints-kurdish-leader-mazloum-abdi-as-presidential-adviser--c1507ae482bc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260827-syria-president-appoints-kurdish-leader-mazloum-abdi-as-presidential-adviser" /><summary type="html">Syrian President Ahmed al-Sharaa appointed Kurdish leader Mazloum Abdi as an adviser to the presidency, state media said on Friday. Abdi's appointment comes just days after he dissolved the Kurdish-led Syrian Democratic Forces (SDF) as part of an integration agreement with Damascus.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran, Qatar hold Hormuz talks as US blockade squeezes Iran oil exports</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f97cebb1b67518c146139be258fef4d3873c1bb6d53521b0e40a8506dd7d018</id><updated>2026-09-01T05:21:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T12:01:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260827-iran-qatar-hold-hormuz-talks-as-us-blockade-chokes-iran-oil-imports--6823e5b7309d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260827-iran-qatar-hold-hormuz-talks-as-us-blockade-chokes-iran-oil-imports" /><summary type="html">Officials from Iran and Qatar met on Thursday in Tehran for diplomatic talks on the strategic Strait of Hormuz, as a US naval blockade chokes oil supplies to Iran amid a domestic shortfall. The meetings follow a week of intense diplomacy in Iran involving separate meetings with officials from Oman and Pakistani seeking ways to end the war and reopen Hormuz.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Driven by faith, Jewish activists stand up to settlers to protect West Bank Palestinians</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8b20f3a846776ae5a56ebbce618fa76c6262975616d1785133c06a2a836e1616</id><updated>2026-09-01T05:21:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-27T09:41:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260827-driven-by-faith-jewish-activists-stand-up-to-settlers-to-protect-west-bank-palestinians--d5b96a52f18a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260827-driven-by-faith-jewish-activists-stand-up-to-settlers-to-protect-west-bank-palestinians" /><summary type="html">A group of Israelis who regularly travel to the West Bank to protect Palestinians who are victims of increasing attacks by settlers say their Jewish faith drove them towards activism. On Tuesday, at least five activists were injured while rushing to assist Palestinians being harassed by settlers in the village of Jannatah, near Bethlehem.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Navigation, jurisdiction, costs: Iran, Oman attempt to hammer out Hormuz deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d53f31c0c6cb09e59213f18c5e9e87c31d0de06bfe4653e31f21a1c643c1749b</id><updated>2026-09-01T05:21:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-26T20:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260826-navigation-jurisdiction-costs-iran-oman-attempt-to-hammer-out-hormuz-deal--a233044920da.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260826-navigation-jurisdiction-costs-iran-oman-attempt-to-hammer-out-hormuz-deal" /><summary type="html">Iran and Oman are holding talks to try to reach an interim agreement for a controlled resumption of navigation in the Strait of Hormuz. The two countries have discussed a framework for a “temporary corridor” for shipping, according to a joint statement by the Iranian and Omani foreign ministries. But the plan faces several hurdles.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Syria: Why is the dissolution of the Kurdish forces significant?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d46471279eb14c73a3aa790172cc25cc87874f845d2b32d0e1b020dd2ec508cd</id><updated>2026-09-01T05:21:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-26T16:16:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260826-syria-why-is-the-dissolution-of-the-kurdish-forces-significant--a05f8cfc7a2c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260826-syria-why-is-the-dissolution-of-the-kurdish-forces-significant" /><summary type="html">The Syrian Kurdish Forces announced their dissolution on August 25, in what is considered a significant step for Syria. FRANCE 24's Andrew Hilliar tells us why.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump says he believes Iran’s leader is still alive but 'seriously wounded'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0b785681b790edf1920246b706e84f99bf2e77920d02068df6caea92a8b15412</id><updated>2026-09-01T05:21:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-26T06:04:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260826-middle-east-live-iran-says-hormuz-strait-still-closed-despite-transit-corridor-talks-with-o--b561458c24a9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260826-middle-east-live-iran-says-hormuz-strait-still-closed-despite-transit-corridor-talks-with-oman" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump on Wednesday said he believes Iran’s Supreme Leader Mojtaba Khamenei is “very seriously wounded”, but not dead. Khamenei has not been seen in public since the US and Israel launched the Iran war in February, prompting months of speculation over the new Iranian leader’s health. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>US-led Gaza peace board warns Hamas over kites after Israeli threat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d8bde9dbab6abbe3d723be3a2129f691644efe58edad5021c29054fa298604a2</id><updated>2026-09-01T05:21:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T21:49:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260825-us-gaza-peace-board-hamas-kites-israeli-threat--526ad678f67e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260825-us-gaza-peace-board-hamas-kites-israeli-threat" /><summary type="html">The US-led board overseeing the Gaza peace plan warned Hamas on Tuesday to halt militant activity, including flying kites, after Israel threatened retaliatory strikes. A Board of Peace official said Israel must also respect the ceasefire, limiting military action to responses to “genuine and imminent threats.”</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Syrian Kurdish leader announces SDF dissolution after its integration into army</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4ada5072121d94041a4095a0272ff78025d62311d0c2581da3714e18b3c2870e</id><updated>2026-09-01T05:21:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T18:49:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260825-syrian-kurdish-leader-dissolves-force-that-spearheaded-jihadist-fight--3b0b10c38d52.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260825-syrian-kurdish-leader-dissolves-force-that-spearheaded-jihadist-fight" /><summary type="html">Mazloum Abdi, the commander-in-chief of the Syrian Kurdish-led Syrian Democratic Forces (SDF) on Tuesday announced the dissolution of the group in a televised speech from the presidential palace in Damascus. The dissolution followed the integration of SDF fighters into the Syrian military, said Abdi, and represented a major victory for Syrian President Ahmed al-Sharaa.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran offers $10 million to kill Trump's son</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7b93b4a07042e8ea6d17240f58b42459ce2ac2feff539028f9726225a2656607</id><updated>2026-09-01T05:21:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T15:44:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/iran-offers-10-million-to-kill-trump-s-son--e32b74674cd9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/iran-offers-10-million-to-kill-trump-s-son" /><summary type="html">Iranian state media has aired a video that appears to threaten the life of Barron Trump, US President Donald Trump's youngest son. Since the start of the war in February, Iranian media have on multiple occasions circulated content threatening the president and family members.  The US Secret Service has confirmed it is aware of the video.</summary></entry><entry><title>US economic D-Day sanctions: 'Repeated bombing attacks across Iran failed to change the calculus'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:51ec5182556b2138c76922b543f9f289ad099f9001019da3c8feccaef920ecbb</id><updated>2026-09-01T05:21:01Z</updated><published>2026-08-25T13:44:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260825-us-economic-d-day-sanctions-repeated-bombing-attacks-across-iran-failed-to-change-the-calcu--31fcda056165.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260825-us-economic-d-day-sanctions-repeated-bombing-attacks-across-iran-failed-to-change-the-calculus" /><summary type="html">Genie Godula is pleased to welcome Imran Bayoumi, Deputy Director &amp; Resident Fellow at the Atlantic Council. He sees the Trump administration’s new sanctions strategy toward Iran as an attempt to seek economic leverage where military force has so far failed to produce any results. But its effectiveness rests on several unresolved assumptions. Chief among them is whether Washington can compel China, Iran’s largest oil customer, to comply despite Beijing’s growing economic resilience. Iran, meanwhile, has decades of experience curtailing sanctions and is again threatening regional escalation.</summary></entry></feed>
